    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58246" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνώδων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οντος</span>, ὁ, in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνώδοντες</span>, two <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>projecting teeth</i> on the blade of a hunting spear,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				10.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.28
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξίφους διπλοῖ κ.</span>, i.e. a
			two-edged sword (cf. Sch.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1233
			</span></i>: sg., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φασγάνου κνώδοντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1374.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνώδων</span> alone, =
			<i>sword</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1025
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				466
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1434
			</span></i>. (Cf. Lith. <i>kándu</i> 'bite').</div>
